        "text": {
            "description_html": "<b>Omnia D11432, Beverly Hills Handleset with Egg Knob</b>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\nThe Beverly Hills Entrance Set is a great way to add a touch of sophisticated beauty to your home. It features an elegant mixture of traditional design with just enough modern flair that it will look great on any front door. It has an egg-shaped knob that adds a point of interest to the handleset. This front door lock will fit door 1-3/4 inches thick to 2 inches thick. Choose from an array of stunning finishes.\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\nAlso available matching <a href=\"/products/beverly-hills-egg-knob-omnia-432-00\">Beverly Hills Egg Knob</a>\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\n<b>Features</b> of the Beverly Hills Egg Knob Entryset:\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Keyway: Schlage \"C\"</li>\r\n<li>Will fit standard 2-1/8\" door preparations.</li>\r\n<li>Will fit narrow stiles. For Door with a 2-3⁄8” backset, stile width can be as narrow as 3-5⁄8”</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\n<b>Specifications</b> for the Omnia D11432 Egg Knob Lockset:\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Material: Brass</li>\r\n<li>Height: 10-5/8\"</li>\r\n<li>Width: 2-3/8\"</li>\r\n<li>Bore Hole Spacing (distance between deadbolt and knob latch): 5-1/2\" Center to Center</li>\r\n<li>Doors Thickness: 1-3/4\" - 2\" Thick Doors (<a href=\"/pages/contact\">Contact Us</a> if doors are thicker)</li></li>\r\n<li>Backset: 2-3/8\" or 2-3/4\"</li>\r\n<li>Deadbolt: Full 1\" Throw, Solid Brass with saw-proof Insert.</li>\r\n<li>Strike: \"T\" strike</li>\r\n<li>Each set contains door knobs, backplates, latches, spindle, and all necessary screws and templates. Key functions are supplied with lock cylinder/s and turnpiece as applicable. </li>\r\n<li><a href=\"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0766/1489/3857/files/entry-lockset-specs.pdf?v=1704262242\" target=\"new\"><b>Omnia Entry Lockset Dimensions & Specs (PDF)</b></a></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\n<b>Available Functions</b> \r\n<ul>\r\n<li><b>Full Dummy Set:</b> Trim for non-working doors. It does not latch and does not lock. Usually used as matching trim for the non-working side of double doors.</li>\r\n<li><b>Single Cylinder:</b> From the exterior, a knob operates the handleset latch and a key operates the deadbolt. From the inside, a thumbturn unlocks the deadbolt and a knob operates the latch.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</p>",
